cryptsetup and LUKS(linux unified keysetup) - disk encryption specification.

info:
    prereq:
        root previlages required.
    description:
        encrypt partitions and disks.
    configuration files:
        /etc/crypttab (Setting up decryption at boot-time) {none, key-slot}
        /etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/ (General path for storing keyfiles)
        /run/cryptsetup/
    binary:
        /usr/bin/cryptsetup
    systemd-files:
        cryptsetup.target
        cryptsetup-pre.target

device="/dev/nvme0n1p4"
partition="/dev/nvme0n1p4"
partition_uuid=$(sudo blkid partition -s UUID -o value).

Encrypt a partition:
    sudo cryptsetup luksFormat partition

Opening a encrypted parition:
    sudo cryptsetup luksOpen/open parition name; (cryptroot)

Adding a keyfile:
    sudo cryptsetup luksAddKey parition path_to_keyfile

Information Dump of a partition:
    sudo cryptsetup luksDump parition

Close the encrypted partition:
    sudo cryptsetup close partition

Open an encrypted partition using a keyfile:
    sudo cryptsetup open partition name --key-file filepath

Open an encrypted partition with a key-slot:
    sudo cryptsetup open partition name --key-slot slot-number

Removing a key-slot:
    sudo cryptsetup luksKillSlot partition slot-number

misc:
    Generating a keyfile (decryption at boot-time):
        sudo dd if=/dev/urandom of=/etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/swap.key bs=512 count=1 status=progress
        sudo chown root:root /etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/swap.key
        sudo chmod 400 /etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/swap.key

----

crypttab configuration - configuration for encrypted block devices.
     The  /etc/crypttab  file describes encrypted block devices that are set up
     during system boot.

    format:
         volume-name encrypted-device key-file options

vim /etc/crypttab:
  crypt_swap UUID=partition_uuid pathToKeyfile none luks,key-slot=1,timeout=1m
  crypt_home UUID=uuid none noauto,swap
  crypt_ro UUID=uuid none readonly

none/blank/- - checks for keyfile at /etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/crypt_home.key or /run/cryptsetup/crypt_home.key
timeout - timeout for password query(0 i.e indefinite is the default, timeout in seconds)
